scription (the latter says one execution counter, with the threshold carried by each instruction). The task instruction takes precedence for this implementation; the difference needs reconciliation before claiming PHP parity. The registry, lexical site selection, directive handling, dispatch, generator behavior, and linked site-set publication/derivation have not been implemented.\\n\\nFixture chronology: the predecessor recorded sequence, loop-body, function-call and generator-resume red with empty output, and the include case timed out. No fixture was turned green in this session. All fixtures retain \\\"'`:oracle :pending`; Docker was not run. The linked include handoff remains unimplemented; no new include run was attempted. The predecessor'\\\"'s exact isolated command \\\"'`timeout 90 clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.ticks-test -v yang.php.antlr.ticks-test/include-handoff-test` timed out after 90 seconds; its combined run timed out after 120 seconds.\\n\\nSequential gates in this session:\\n\\n| Gate | Result | Duration |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.safepoint-test` | pass, 9 tests / 20 assertions | 3.802 s |\\n| `cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | pass | 0.2 s |\\n| `clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | 0 errors, 0 warnings | 6.5 s |\\n| PHP tick, lowering, prelude and e2e; Python trace gates | not run in this session | — |\\n\\nThe requested implementation and acceptance gates remain outstanding. Earlier green and timeout results are recorded in part B'\\\"'s findings; they are not new results from this session.\\nEOF\\n\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:45:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git add src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md && git commit -m 'feat(php): declare statement ticks profile' && git push\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:46:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git add src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md && git commit -m 'feat(php): declare statement ticks profile' && git push\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Running formatters on staged files...\\nFormatting complete.\\n[p7b-ticks 38375bf7] feat(php): declare statement ticks profile\\n 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)\\n create mode 100644 collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\\nTo github.com:sonwh98/datomworld.git\\n   411c2b08..38375bf7  p7b-ticks -> p7b-ticks\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:47:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"**The PHP ticks integration is incomplete.** I added the independent `:after` ticks profile and pushed it in commit `38375bf7`, but it is not wired into execution. The staged fixtures remain red; the registry, statement-site lowering, firing rule, generator behavior, and linked include handoff are still outstanding.\\n\\nThe shared safepoint test passed (9 tests, 20 assertions), and the touched source file passed cljstyle and kondo. I did not run the PHP or Python gates in this session.\\n\\nThe task specifies a counter per `declare` site, while the cited slice-3 design describes a request-wide counter. The explicit task instruction takes precedence for implementation; I recorded the discrepancy for parity review.\\n\\nDetails and the predecessor’s include timeout command are in the [part C findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p7b/collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md).\"}}\n---\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\n\n## Delegation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Lead System Architect\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\n\nRead first:\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\n- <target-design-file>\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\n\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
