{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1920,1960p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '2095,2125p' docs/design/yang.php.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc | head -90; rg -n 'p7|docker|defn -main' scripts/*php* src/dev/*php* test/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj; rg -n 'shiva|Get the code' docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -25; command -v php; command -v docker; rg --files /Users/sto/workspace | rg 'zend_(execute|compile|vm_def|globals)' | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1920,1960p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '2095,2125p' docs/design/yang.php.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc | head -90; rg -n 'p7|docker|defn -main' scripts/*php* src/dev/*php* test/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj; rg -n 'shiva|Get the code' docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -25; command -v php; command -v docker; rg --files /Users/sto/workspace | rg 'zend_(execute|compile|vm_def|globals)' | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"   `:yang.php/refusal`.\n\n## 12. Safepoints\n\n- `:loop` and `:call` hooks (`phpsp`) serve signals: `pcntl_signal` handlers\n  run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, and\n  `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode. A recursion-depth bound\n  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off).\n- `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP and so\n  nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count\n  budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text, a recorded departure\n  (owner decision B8.5, corner C21). A composition may supply one non-negative\n  integer budget per run; omission means unlimited. Each entry to a `:loop` or\n  `:call` hook consumes one unit, and the hook after the last available unit\n  raises `PHP Fatal error:  Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded`.\n  This operational fatal is not guest-catchable and skips shutdown functions\n  and destructors. It bounds execution between hooks, not wall-clock time or\n  blocking host operations; no generic VM instructions are charged.\n- **Statement ticks** (`declare(ticks=N)`, `register_tick_function`) need\n  `:line` sites before non-lambda statement nodes. `yang.safepoint` currently\n  refuses a selected site that is not a `:lambda` (`site-not-lambda`), and\n  `:line` insertion is safepoint slice 3, which Python tracing also needs.\n  Ticks therefore **depend on the shared `:line` extension**: P7 splits into\n  P7-a (signals, no dependency) and P7-b (ticks, behind safepoint slice 3).\n  Neither L1 to L4 nor this frontend extends `yang.safepoint`; the extension\n  is the safepoint seat's.\n- No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded, and one request is one task.\n\n## 13. Diagnostics\n\nCompile time: `:yang.php/syntax`; `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}`;\n`:yang.php/not-php`; `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` (a warning);\n`:yang.php/compile-error` for PHP's compile-time fatals (a function redeclared\nin one unit, `break 0`, a duplicate parameter, `$this` reassignment, a\npositional argument after a named one). Run time: guest warnings, notices and\ndeprecations as records on the guest-diagnostics stream; fatals as `Error`\nthrows; the uncaught-exception text pinned. Operational failures stay\noperational (`yang.antlr.md` section 11).\n\n## 14. The differential-corpus plan\n\n|       |                                  | `include` warns and yields        |\n|       |                                  | `false`, `require` and            |\n|       |                                  | `require_once` throw `Error`; a   |\n|       |                                  | refused `_once` retries delivery  |\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n| P7-a  | signals: `phpsp` hooks at        | a signal at a `:loop` hook runs   |\n|       | `:loop` and `:call`,             | the handler; an empty signal      |\n|       | `pcntl_signal`, the safepoint    | stream never parks; budget        |\n|       | budget                           | exhaustion raises the pinned      |\n|       |                                  | fatal text                        |\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n| P7-b  | ticks: `declare(ticks)`,         | tick counts equal PHP's for the   |\n|       | `register_tick_function`; behind | statement fixture                 |\n|       | safepoint slice 3                |                                   |\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n| P8    | legacy retirement: the legacy    | the REPL prints `1` for `<?php $x |\n|       | test programs in the new corpus, | = 1; echo $x;`; every legacy test |\n|       | the demo on checked-in CST       | program passes with corrected     |\n|       | packets,                         | expectations; the demo runs its   |\n|       | `src/dev/subsystems.edn`         | samples parserless in the         |\n|       | retargeted, `yang/php.cljc`      | browser; no reference to the      |\n|       | deleted, the compiler revision   | legacy `yang.php` namespace       |\n|       | removed from the standard        | remains                           |\n|       | catalog                          |                                   |\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n| P9    | builtin surface slices (strings  | each a corpus group with PHP      |\n|       | II, arrays II, JSON, math II),   | parity; `eval` shares the         |\n|       | `$$`, `extract`, `compact` and   | caller's symbol table; closes     |\n|       | the dynamic scope, `eval` as a   | corners C5, C6 (prefer-ref), C11, |\n|       | compilation request              | C12, C13                          |\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n     1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.safepoint\n     2\t  \"The PHP `:loop` and `:call` hooks. A bounded run charges one safepoint to\n     3\t   its per-run counter; exhaustion unwinds past guest handlers and raises the\n     4\t   operational fatal, not a guest Throwable.\"\n     5\t  (:require\n     6\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n     7\t\n     8\t\n     9\t(def profile\n    10\t  {:loop 'php.sp/loop, :call {:hook 'php.sp/call, :sequence true}})\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t(def ticks-profile\n    14\t  \"Statement completion hooks for PHP's lexical ticks directives. This is\n    15\t   separate from the execution-budget profile so ticks do not charge it.\"\n    16\t  {:line {:hook 'php.sp/line, :operands true, :after true}})\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t(def fatal-text\n    20\t  \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\")\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\t(def ^:private function-definitions\n    24\t  '[[php.sp/exhaust!\n    25\t     ;; the terminal root escape: guest handlers, returns and finalizers\n    26\t     ;; cannot replace the operational fatal\n    27\t     (fn []\n    28\t       (php/root-fatal \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\"))]\n    29\t    [php.sp/tick\n    30\t     (fn []\n    31\t       (let [n (cell/get php.sp/remaining)]\n    32\t         (if (= n 0)\n    33\t           (php.sp/exhaust!)\n    34\t           (do (cell/set! php.sp/remaining (- n 1)) :php/null))))]\n    35\t    [php.sp/loop (fn [] (php.sp/tick))]\n    36\t    [php.sp/call (fn [] (php.sp/tick))]])\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- definitions->uast\n    40\t  [defs]\n    41\t  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn program\n    45\t  \"The bounded run: hook definitions and a counter holding `budget`, then the\n    46\t   safepoint-derived program `ast`. `budget` must be a non-negative integer;\n    47\t   anything else is a named host-side error, not a guest diagnostic.\"\n    48\t  [budget ast]\n    49\t  (when-not (and (integer? budget) (not (neg? budget)))\n    50\t    (throw (ex-info \"php.sp/remaining budget must be a non-negative integer\"\n    51\t                    {:yang.php.antlr.safepoint/error :invalid-budget\n    52\t                     :budget budget})))\n    53\t  (u/mark-tails\n    54\t    (u/then (definitions->uast function-definitions)\n    55\t            (u/then (u/def! 'php.sp/remaining (u/sexp->uast (list 'cell/new budget)))\n    56\t                    ast))))\nzsh:1: no matches found: scripts/*php*\n53:# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n127:`test:sub`. As in the shiva script below, currently unowned namespaces run\n205:jupiter 5,645 s at 12 workers, shiva comparable). Do not run another lane\n394:  disjoint lane pair (`src/dev/nightly.clj`): **jupiter takes the jvm lane, shiva\n395:  takes node and dart** (each lane in its own clone; shiva publishes the run pin,\n413:| Full JVM lane, one process, before tagging (shiva) | 70 min |\n416:| **Slow tier (shiva, one JVM per namespace, 6 at a time)** | **53 min**, 22 namespaces, 168 tests, all exit 0; longest `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` 3183 s (about 1580 s alone on the laptop) |\n502:## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n510:| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n511:| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). mise was moved off the apt package to the official user-local install (`~/.local/bin/mise`, 2026.11.2, owner action 2026-11-07) so both hosts share shiva's layout; toolchains in `~/.local/share/mise/installs/` were untouched. Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n514:that is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\n532:### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n542:ssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n557:refs. Measured on shiva 2026-11-02: the `dg` clone was created from the `p4`\n586:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\n605:average over 100 on 2026-11-01; the remote hosts own that tier. On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\n624:The first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\n638:command line (shiva: `node,dart` + `--pin-publish`; jupiter: `jvm` +\n639:`--pin-read --pin-peer shiva...`) is the only difference.\n648:   the measured miss on shiva 2026-11-02: the cljs lane ran but the\n716:  sit far inside jupiter's 48 cores / 62 GB and shiva's 24 / 62;\n800:  on shiva: the namespace passes 5/5.\n803:- Both hosts run other work (a QEMU guest and rustdesk on shiva); idle load is\n817:  shiva and jupiter, hourly cron plus a 04:00 Vietnam guard and flock,\n820:  the JVM full suite on jupiter, the full Node and Dart suites on shiva.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
