{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files src/dev | rg 'php|oracle'; nl -ba test/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj; sed -n '502,540p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n 'p7|shiva|oracle' collab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p7b-ticks-b.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md; rg --files -g AGENTS.md collab docs test src\"","aggregated_output":"src/dev/jolt_j0c_oracle.clj\nsrc/dev/yang_ts_oracle_preload.cjs\nsrc/dev/yang_ts_oracle.clj\nsrc/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj\nsrc/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj\nsrc/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj\nsrc/dev/yang/php/corpus.clj\nsrc/dev/yang/php/phpt.clj\nsrc/dev/yang/php/oracle_test.clj\nsrc/dev/dao/space/datomic_query_oracle.clj\n     1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.ticks-test\n     2\t  (:require\n     3\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     4\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n     5\t    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\n     6\t    [yang.php.antlr.linked-harness :as lh]\n     7\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p7b :as p7b]))\n     8\t\n     9\t\n    10\t(deftest tick-fixtures-test\n    11\t  (doseq [{:keys [id source out units]} p7b/fixtures\n    12\t          :when (nil? units)]\n    13\t    (testing (name id)\n    14\t      (is (= out (:php/out (h/run-raw (str \"<?php \" p7b/prologue source))))))))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(deftest include-handoff-test\n    18\t  (let [{:keys [source units out]} (last p7b/fixtures)\n    19\t        packets (update-vals (assoc units \"main.php\" (str \"<?php \" p7b/prologue source))\n    20\t                             cst/parse-source)\n    21\t        result (lh/run-fixture packets \"main.php\" {})]\n    22\t    (doseq [[vm value] (:values result)]\n    23\t      (is (= out (h/latin1->text (:php/out value))) (name vm)))))\n## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n\nTwo Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\nreached over SSH as `sto` with key authentication, and both have `mise`, `tmux`\nand `git`.\n\n| Host | Cores / RAM | Toolchain state (server snapshot checked 2026-10-11; repo selection comes from `mise.toml`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). mise was moved off the apt package to the official user-local install (`~/.local/bin/mise`, 2026.11.2, owner action 2026-11-07) so both hosts share shiva's layout; toolchains in `~/.local/share/mise/installs/` were untouched. Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n\n**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\nthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\nowner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\n\n### Kill remote processes by exact PID, never by name pattern\n\nOn these hosts, kill a runaway nightly/lane process by its exact PID\n(`pgrep -af <pattern>` only to LIST, then `kill <pid>`), never with\n`pkill -f <string>` / `killall <name>`. Measured 2026-11-06: `pkill -f\n\"nightly.clj\"` over SSH matched the invoking bash command line itself\n(the pattern appears in `ps` output of the session carrying the kill),\nterminating the SSH session mid-command — exit 255 with the kill\nhalf-done. A name-pattern kill also races concurrent seats: another\norchestrator's delegate process whose arguments embed the same string\ndies with yours. If the PID from `pgrep -af` is ambiguous (several\ncandidates), inspect with `ps -o pid,etime,args -p <pid>` first and kill\nthe exact process; a session that dies under you is a symptom of this\nmistake, not a host outage.\n\n### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n\nRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\nwould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\ndirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\nbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\nthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n\n```sh\n3:Branch: p7b-ticks\n10:C. Partial. Five hand-derived, oracle-pending expectations are in `test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p7b.cljc:9`. `test/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj:10` is intentionally red while B is absent. Chronology: sequence was added and run first, producing expected ATTBT vs actual empty output. Loop-body, function-call and generator-resume were then added and run red together: expected ATAT, FT, ATBT respectively, each actual empty. These fail at the missing registration builtin and do not yet isolate count semantics. Include-handoff was initially run without a linked harness (invalid red); it was then moved to the linked-unit harness (`ticks_test.clj:17`) and rerun; both the combined 120-second run and a separate 90-second retry timed out. The include case therefore does not yet have a valid red result. All expectations await oracle confirmation.\n12:D. Partial. `src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj` has a P7 prologue, multi-unit runner and `--p7` group. Its namespace and prologue load successfully; the actual Docker execution is deliberately not run. Its fold provenance remains :pending until the orchestrator records it.\n20:Gate update: the combined PHP/shared safepoint, Python bundled/linked safepoint, and PHP lowering/prelude/e2e JVM commands each timed out after 120 seconds without a result; they were run concurrently and contended for resources. A sequential retry of `yang.safepoint-test` passed 9 tests / 20 assertions; a sequential JVM retry of Python `trace-basic-test` passed 1 test / 4 assertions. A sequential JVM retry of Python `linked-tracing-profile-test` passed 1 test / 3 assertions. The linked include red run timed out after 120 seconds and its isolated retry after 90 seconds; neither established a valid include red. The P7 oracle runner's multi-unit preparation and working directory were checked with a mocked `clojure.java.shell/sh`; no Docker ran. Commit `752359df` was pushed. Its tests remain deliberately failing while B is absent.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
