{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj | sed -n '1,200p'; rg -n -- 'p7|--p7|spit|main|docker' src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj; sed -n '245,300p' collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-architect-safepoint-slice3-design.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md; rg -n 'ticks_count|zend_compile' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld*/collab/yang-php/*findings.md | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.php.oracle\n     2\t  \"PHP 8.3 CLI oracle runner for `yang.php.antlr.programs`\n     3\t   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 14, 17.3).\n     4\t\n     5\t   For every fixture in `programs/fixtures` (plus `matrix-source` and\n     6\t   `float-cases`), writes the PHP source to a temporary file and runs:\n     7\t     docker run --rm -v <dir>:/w -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\n     8\t       -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\n     9\t       -d log_errors=0 <file>\n    10\t   Parses stdout into `:out`, `:diag` (`[[errno message] ...]`) and `:uncaught`\n    11\t   (`{:class c :message m}`), and compares against each fixture's expectation\n    12\t   (or `:departure/:zend` for departure fixtures).\"\n    13\t  (:require\n    14\t    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    15\t    [clojure.java.shell :as sh]\n    16\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    17\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\n    18\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\n    19\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\n    20\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]\n    21\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5b2 :as p5b2]\n    22\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p6 :as p6]\n    23\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p7b :as p7b])\n    24\t  (:import\n    25\t    (java.nio.charset\n    26\t      StandardCharsets)\n    27\t    (java.nio.file\n    28\t      Files)\n    29\t    (java.nio.file.attribute\n    30\t      FileAttribute)))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(def banner\n    34\t  \"The pinned PHP 8.3 CLI oracle provenance banner.\"\n    35\t  p3b/banner)\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(def p5-banner\n    39\t  \"The P5 request-context run's own provenance banner (version/host/date of\n    40\t  the P5 recording pass, not P3-b's).\"\n    41\t  \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def ^:private errno-of\n    45\t  {\"Warning\" 2,\n    46\t   \"Notice\" 8,\n    47\t   \"Deprecated\" 8192,\n    48\t   \"Fatal error\" 1})\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn class-derived?\n    52\t  \"Whether the recorded diag entry carries a class-derived errno: the runner\n    53\t  parses only the `Warning|Notice|...` kind line, so the recorded number is\n    54\t  derived from the message class, not the true constant (e.g. `Notice` parses\n    55\t  to 8 where the engine's semantic truth for `E_USER_NOTICE` is 1024).\"\n    56\t  [diag-entry]\n    57\t  (boolean (:yang.php.oracle/class-derived (meta diag-entry))))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- mark-class-derived\n    61\t  \"Mark a recorded `[errno message]` pair as class-derived (see [[class-derived?]]).\"\n    62\t  [pair]\n    63\t  (with-meta pair {:yang.php.oracle/class-derived true}))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn errno-match?\n    67\t  \"Whether expected errno `e` matches recorded diag entry `a`: identical\n    68\t  numbers match, and a class-derived parse mismatch counts as equal ONLY when\n    69\t  the oracle record is marked class-derived (the runner parses only the\n    70\t  `Warning|Notice|...` kind line: E_USER_NOTICE parses to 8 and E_USER_WARNING\n    71\t  to 2 where the engine's semantic truth is 1024 and 512).\"\n    72\t  [e a]\n    73\t  (let [[actual-errno] a]\n    74\t    (or (= e actual-errno)\n    75\t        (and (= 1024 e) (= 8 actual-errno) (class-derived? a))\n    76\t        (and (= 512 e) (= 2 actual-errno) (class-derived? a)))))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn diag-match?\n    80\t  \"Whether the expected diag vector matches the recorded one entry-wise under\n    81\t  [[errno-match?]] (messages compare literally).\"\n    82\t  [expected-diag actual-diag]\n    83\t  (and (= (count expected-diag) (count actual-diag))\n    84\t       (every? true? (map (fn [[e-errno e-msg] a]\n    85\t                            (and (errno-match? e-errno a)\n    86\t                                 (= e-msg (second a))))\n    87\t                          expected-diag actual-diag))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- location-pattern\n    91\t  \"The regex source of a PHP source location below `/w/`: the entry `file`\n    92\t   itself, or, for a multi-unit fixture run in `/w/<unit-dir>`, any unit file\n    93\t   below the directory.\"\n    94\t  [file unit-dir]\n    95\t  (if unit-dir\n    96\t    (str (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote unit-dir) \"/[^\\\\s:]+\")\n    97\t    (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote file)))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- strip-location\n   101\t  ([s file] (strip-location s file nil))\n   102\t  ([s file unit-dir]\n   103\t   (str/replace s\n   104\t                (re-pattern (str \" in /w/\" (location-pattern file unit-dir) \" on line \\\\d+\"))\n   105\t                \"\")))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn parse-stdout\n   109\t  \"Parse PHP CLI stdout for `/w/<file>` into\n   110\t   `{:out <string> :diag [[errno msg] ...] :uncaught {:class c :message m}-or-nil}`.\n   111\t   With `unit-dir`, locations in any file below `/w/<unit-dir>` are stripped\n   112\t   (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n   113\t  ([raw file] (parse-stdout raw file nil))\n   114\t  ([raw file unit-dir]\n   115\t   (let [qfile (location-pattern file unit-dir)\n   116\t         strip-location (fn [s file] (strip-location s file unit-dir))\n   117\t         ;; The uncaught block ends at PHP's own terminator, so output written\n   118\t         ;; after it (shutdown functions, destructors) stays in :out.\n   119\t         uncaught-re (re-pattern\n   120\t                       (str \"(?s)\\\\nFatal error: Uncaught ([^:]+): ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*) in /w/\"\n   121\t                            qfile\n   122\t                            \":\\\\d+\\\\nStack trace:\\\\n.*?\\\\n  thrown in /w/\"\n   123\t                            qfile\n   124\t                            \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n   125\t         fatal-re (re-pattern\n   126\t                    (str \"\\\\nFatal error: ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*) in /w/\"\n   127\t                         qfile\n   128\t                         \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n   129\t         diag-re (re-pattern\n   130\t                   (str \"\\\\n(Warning|Notice|Deprecated): ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*?) in /w/\"\n   131\t                        qfile\n   132\t                        \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n   133\t         [without-fatal uncaught fatal]\n   134\t         (if-let [[_ cls msg] (re-find uncaught-re raw)]\n   135\t           [(str/replace raw uncaught-re \"\")\n   136\t            {:class cls, :message (strip-location msg file)}\n   137\t            nil]\n   138\t           (if-let [[_ msg] (re-find fatal-re raw)]\n   139\t             ;; a plain (non-uncaught-exception) fatal: the engine's\n   140\t             ;; guest-fatal representation (`:php/fatal message`, shutdown\n   141\t             ;; already run) is preserved as `:fatal`, and `:uncaught`\n   142\t             ;; stays nil — a plain fatal populates one slot only.\n   143\t             [(str/replace raw fatal-re \"\")\n   144\t              nil\n   145\t              (strip-location msg file)]\n   146\t             [raw nil nil]))\n   147\t         diags (volatile! [])\n   148\t         out (str/replace without-fatal\n   149\t                          diag-re\n   150\t                          (fn [[_ kind msg]]\n   151\t                            (vswap! diags conj (mark-class-derived [(get errno-of kind) (strip-location msg file)]))\n   152\t                            \"\"))]\n   153\t     ;; a single-slot plain fatal carries its own diagnostic: the engine\n   154\t     ;; records the fatal's E_USER_ERROR-class diagnostic (errno 256)\n   155\t     ;; alongside `:fatal`, so `:diag` carries it too.\n   156\t     {:out out,\n   157\t      :diag (if fatal (conj @diags [256 fatal]) @diags),\n   158\t      :uncaught uncaught,\n   159\t      :fatal fatal})))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn run-php-file\n   163\t  \"Run `<file>` inside `<dir>` via Docker `php:8.3-cli` and return the parsed\n   164\t   `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`. With `unit-dir`, the working directory is\n   165\t   `/w/<unit-dir>` and `file` is relative to it (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n   166\t  ([dir file] (run-php-file dir file nil))\n   167\t  ([dir file unit-dir]\n   168\t   (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\n   169\t         (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n   170\t                \"-v\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \":/w\")\n   171\t                \"-w\" (if unit-dir (str \"/w/\" unit-dir) \"/w\")\n   172\t                \"php:8.3-cli\" \"php\"\n   173\t                \"-d\" \"display_errors=1\"\n   174\t                \"-d\" \"html_errors=0\"\n   175\t                \"-d\" \"error_reporting=E_ALL\"\n   176\t                \"-d\" \"log_errors=0\"\n   177\t                file\n   178\t                :out-enc \"UTF-8\")]\n   179\t     (assoc (parse-stdout out (if unit-dir (str unit-dir \"/\" file) file) unit-dir)\n   180\t            :err err\n   181\t            :exit exit))))\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\t(defn- write-source!\n   185\t  [dir file ^String source]\n   186\t  (Files/write (.toPath (io/file dir file))\n   187\t               (.getBytes source StandardCharsets/UTF_8)\n   188\t               (make-array java.nio.file.OpenOption 0)))\n   189\t\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn- unit-actual\n   192\t  \"Run the multi-unit `fixture`: every unit is written below `<dir>/<id>/`,\n   193\t   `main.php` is run with that directory as the working directory, and\n   194\t   `/w/<id>` is replaced by `.` in everything the program printed (the\n   195\t   comparison's definition, plan P6 2.5 rule 2; corner C37).\"\n   196\t  [dir {:keys [id units main], :or {main \"main.php\"}}]\n   197\t  (let [unit-dir (name id)\n   198\t        norm (fn [s] (str/replace s (str \"/w/\" unit-dir) \".\"))]\n   199\t    (doseq [[path source] units]\n   200\t      (let [f (io/file dir unit-dir path)]\n7:     docker run --rm -v <dir>:/w -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\n23:    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p7b :as p7b])\n169:         (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n193:   `main.php` is run with that directory as the working directory, and\n196:  [dir {:keys [id units main], :or {main \"main.php\"}}]\n203:    (let [actual (run-php-file dir main unit-dir)]\n376:         (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n473:(defn p7-prologue\n476:  (str \"<?php \" p7b/prologue))\n479:(defn check-p7-fixture\n484:    (doseq [[path contents] (merge units {\"main.php\" (str \"<?php \" source),\n485:                                          \"pre.php\" (p7-prologue)})]\n489:    (let [actual (run-php-file-with-prepend dir \"main.php\" pre unit-dir)\n498:(defn run-p7\n501:  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-p7-\"\n504:      (mapv #(check-p7-fixture dir %) p7b/fixtures)\n539:(defn -main\n549:      ;; Dry run: no docker, no oracle. Print the generated prologue for\n558:  (when (some #{\"--p7\"} args)\n559:    (let [results (run-p7)\n\nPassing that gate unblocks PHP P7-b. P7-b itself remains incomplete until its tick semantics and linked-unit acceptance pass. Eval execution fixtures remain P9 work.\n\n**6. Implementation slices, seats, and ordering**\n\n| Order | Seat | Files and work |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Architect + safepoint owner | Reconcile stale status in `docs/design/yang.php.md` §12 and `docs/design/yang.antlr.md` §8.5.2; specify `:after`, payloads, retention, and acceptance. |\n| 2 | Shared safepoint compiler seat | `src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc`: add validated after-placement, value-preserving rewrite, and provenance-path handling. Reserve the result binder in `src/cljc/yang/core/names.cljc`. Add focused cases to `test/yang/safepoint_test.cljc`. |\n| 3 | QA/verification seat | Run shared cross-host derivation checks and existing Python bundled/linked tracing regressions. Establish the shared landing gate. |\n| 4 | PHP compiler/runtime seat | `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc`: lexical directive tracking and completion-site selection. `safepoint.cljc`: distinct statement-tick hooks and bundled/linked emission. `prelude.cljc`: request-owned state and builtin wiring. Extend PHP safepoint fixtures. |\n| 5 | Publication/linker integration seat | Enable the existing publication `:site-set` seam in PHP; add a PHP site-set adapter, verified link-time derivation, hook dependency pins, and SCC alias rebinding. Extend include and portable publication fixtures. |\n| 6 | QA + independent reviewer | Record pinned PHP oracle results; verify consumer semantics, lifecycle, bundle sizes, and the required host/evaluator lanes. Review shared and PHP completion separately. |\n| Later | P9 eval seat | Feed each admitted eval compilation through the same site/profiling contract and add eval-boundary fixtures. |\n\nThe shared insertion change belongs to the safepoint seat, as PHP explicitly requires at [yang.php.md:1944](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.php.md:1944). Python needs regression coverage for this work; its existing tracing implementation does not need to be rebuilt.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
