{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.prompt.md | sed -n '12,28p'; nl -ba src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj | sed -n '479,508p'; rg -n 'oracle|p7' deps.edn bb.edn | head -25; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc | sed -n '30,55p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc | sed -n '145,170p'\"","aggregated_output":"    12\t2. Part B's findings (collab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p7b-ticks-b.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md):\n    13\t   staged-red fixtures (programs_p7b.cljc, ticks_test.clj), the oracle p7 group (D), and the\n    14\t   environment/gate lessons — CRITICAL: its concurrent 120s lane runs all timed out; run\n    15\t   SEQUENTIALLY with generous timeouts (300-600s each, the prelude compile chain is minutes).\n    16\t3. Design authority: docs/design/yang.php.md §12 + §15 P7-b row + collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-architect-safepoint-slice3-design.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md (the :after profile shape is ALREADY implemented in the shared core at src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:153 — part A; do not re-litigate it).\n    17\t\n    18\t## Implement (B from the original brief)\n    19\t- declare(ticks=N) pragma: lowering recognizes the directive, marks statement sites under the ticks profile using the NEW :after capability {:line {:hook php.sp/line :operands true :after true}} (site selection per the design; remember derivation validates invalid combinations).\n    20\t- register_tick_function / unregister_tick_function builtins (registry + the tick firing rule: every N marked statements on NORMAL completion; a count is per declare-site, PHP semantics; generator resume fires the pending after-hook exactly when its statement completes — the design's table).\n    21\t- include site-set handoff: canonical published rows carry no marks; PHP receives the unit explicitly (design's landing requirement). The include red currently TIMES OUT — if your implementation doesn't fix the timeout in a reasonable budget, mark it in findings with the exact command + durations rather than leaving it hanging; the orchestrator reruns it remote if needed.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Gates (all sequential, generous timeouts)\n    24\t- ticks_test + yang.php tick/lowering/prelude focused namespaces green; yang.safepoint-test 9/20 stays green; python trace-basic + linked-tracing-profile green (additivity); affected e2e fast set; kondo 0/0 + cljstyle clean on touched files. Fixtures stay :oracle :pending — do NOT run docker.\n    25\t\n    26\t## Rules\n    27\t- Conventional commits on p7b-ticks; push as you go. No merges. Design gap -> stop that item + report.\n    28\t- Findings: collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md (per-fixture red->green chronology, file:line, gate table with sequential timings, include-handoff status).\n   479\t(defn check-p7-fixture\n   480\t  \"Run a P7 fixture with its prologue and optional included units.\"\n   481\t  [dir {:keys [id source units out oracle]}]\n   482\t  (let [unit-dir (name id)\n   483\t        pre (str unit-dir \"/pre.php\")]\n   484\t    (doseq [[path contents] (merge units {\"main.php\" (str \"<?php \" source),\n   485\t                                          \"pre.php\" (p7-prologue)})]\n   486\t      (let [f (io/file dir unit-dir path)]\n   487\t        (io/make-parents f)\n   488\t        (write-source! dir (str unit-dir \"/\" path) contents)))\n   489\t    (let [actual (run-php-file-with-prepend dir \"main.php\" pre unit-dir)\n   490\t          expected {:out out, :diag [], :uncaught nil}]\n   491\t      {:id id, :oracle oracle,\n   492\t       :pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n   493\t                   (= expected (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught]))),\n   494\t       :expected expected,\n   495\t       :actual (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught :fatal]) :exit (:exit actual))})))\n   496\t\n   497\t\n   498\t(defn run-p7\n   499\t  \"Run the pending P7-b ticks fixtures against php:8.3-cli.\"\n   500\t  []\n   501\t  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-p7-\"\n   502\t                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n   503\t    (try\n   504\t      (mapv #(check-p7-fixture dir %) p7b/fixtures)\n   505\t      (finally\n   506\t        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n   507\t          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n   508\t\ndeps.edn:35:                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\ndeps.edn:98:           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\ndeps.edn:121:           ;; Development/oracle only (datomic-q-v1 Client oracle runner,\ndeps.edn:124:           :oracle {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\" \"test\"]\ndeps.edn:126:                                 ;; oracle backend: Datomic Local, in-process,\ndeps.edn:127:                                 ;; run in docker/oracle (dev-scope only)\nbb.edn:116:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:219:  {:doc \"J1 DIAGNOSTIC, not the oracle verdict: dao.host.float-test and dao.host.text-test, unchanged, under jolt with the :jolt-diag stand-in for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures (isolates these checks from the real corpus loader); see src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc\"\n    30\t                     (if (class-map? unit)\n    31\t                       (lower/classmap-paths unit)\n    32\t                       (lower/imported-unit-names packet {:path name}))),\n    33\t   :module-spec (fn [registry {:keys [name packet strict-types], :as unit} php-address deps]\n    34\t                  (if (class-map? unit)\n    35\t                    (lower/classmap-spec registry unit php-address deps)\n    36\t                    (lower/module-spec registry packet\n    37\t                                       {:path name,\n    38\t                                        :strict-types strict-types,\n    39\t                                        :php-address php-address,\n    40\t                                        :deps deps}))),\n    41\t   :scc-module-specs lower/scc-module-specs,\n    42\t   :site-set nil,\n    43\t   :binder-table nil,\n    44\t   :refusal-ns \"yang.php\",\n    45\t   :publish-fn publish-fn})\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn publication-order\n    49\t  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the input order for acyclic units.\n    50\t   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n    51\t   publication step per SCC. An include edge no unit and no `published`\n    52\t   entry supplies is refused `:yang.php/unpublished-import` by name.\"\n    53\t  [units published]\n    54\t  (core/publication-order (config publish/publish-module!) units published))\n    55\t\n   145\t(defn- sequence-hook\n   146\t  \"`node` evaluated after `hook` is applied.\"\n   147\t  [node hook]\n   148\t  {:type :application,\n   149\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [binder], :body node},\n   150\t   :operands [(hook-application hook [])]})\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- after-hook\n   154\t  [node hook]\n   155\t  {:type :application,\n   156\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [result-binder],\n   157\t              :body (sequence-hook {:type :variable, :name result-binder} hook)},\n   158\t   :operands [node]})\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\t(defn- prefix-hook\n   162\t  \"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied before its body runs.\"\n   163\t  [node hook]\n   164\t  (assoc node\n   165\t         :body (sequence-hook (:body node) hook)))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn- wrap-hook\n   169\t  \"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied to its body's value.\"\n   170\t  [node hook]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
